Z||000000||Shiner||02-20-2000||11:00 PM||||I tried posting this in "the mall" but go no responses.  Here it goes, I am in need of a front fascia for my '87 GT (which means it needs round trim)  It must have no cracks, and it must not be deformed in any way.  Paint condition does not matter, because I am painting my car.  It would cost too much to ship it, so I would like to pick it up.  I live about 20min SOUTH of Easton, PA, or about an hour north of Philadelphia.  If anybody has one (within, say, a 3 hour drive), or knows where I can get one, LMK!||||reg||11
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-21-2000||11:55 AM||||Hey me too! I need a facia for an 86 SE V6! and passenger side front 1/4... its all cracked and crappy looking!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||02-21-2000||05:33 PM||||If you can find the front round trim good luck.  I've been told its the first thing that breaks in an accident or when the car gets towed.  I've been looking around for more than a year.  All the Fiero parts places don't have them and Mr Goodwrench say discontinued item.  I do have a nose from my '88, no trim pieces.  It is solid, but had some spider web cracks in the paint from Florida sun or a flexed front.  I was saving it just in case.||||reg||11
Z||000003||batboy||02-21-2000||08:12 PM||||FOCOA lists front facias in their magazine. You may want to call Kick Hill too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shiner||02-21-2000||09:01 PM||||I have looked around at places like Kick Hill.  The problem is that these guys have to make MONEY off of this stuff.  Some of the prices people are asking for this are outrageous!  Personally, I don't think mine can be repaired.  There are several places that would need to be filled and sanded, a part of it is pushed in, and it just generally looks like hell.  Nobody has one for me?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000005||Cooter||02-21-2000||09:05 PM||||I have one off of an 86 GT, but it is rough. It needs stripping and some cracks fixed. I was keeping it "just in case" but if you can't find the perfect one you are looking for, let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000006||superXmotorsports||02-22-2000||10:38 PM||||The last round moulding GT facia I bought was a new GM one in the box for $350. SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||02-23-2000||04:39 AM||||As a last resort, you might try a plastic welder.  I don't think they are terribly expensive and it might just work.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroshop||02-25-2000||10:45 AM||||I have front facia's repaired all the time. In fact what I do is send them out to a bumper repair shop and they reweld the whole cover and strip it at the same time, it comes back to me looking brand new ready for paint as they also prime the cover. If some of you have seen Robert's yeloow GT on mt web site you will see that the front cover looks like it never had problems but in fact it had four rips in several locations.||||reg||6
